1
00:00:08,064 --> 00:00:14,078
Long long ago, in the island of Lanka,
South of ancient India,

2
00:00:14,078 --> 00:00:20,285
lived the evil king Ravana, whose wicked
ambition to conquer and

3
00:00:20,285 --> 00:00:26,687
dominate the whole world, caused pain and
misery to one and all.

4
00:00:27,893 --> 00:00:31,272
And in Kaushala, a kingdom in north India,

5
00:00:31,272 --> 00:00:35,697
people prospered under the benevolent
ruler, Dashrath.

6
00:00:38,904 --> 00:00:42,359
However, Kaushala's capital Ayodhya's
biggest concern

7
00:00:42,359 --> 00:00:44,705
was that King Dashrath had no heir.

8
00:00:46,746 --> 00:00:51,578
On the advice of sage Vashishtha, King
Dashrath performed

9
00:00:51,578 --> 00:00:54,715
a Yajna the ceremony to beget a son.

10
00:00:55,755 --> 00:01:00,721
And as a result he was blessed with four
sons from his three queens.

11
00:01:01,927 --> 00:01:05,874
One of them was Ram, the hero of this
story,

12
00:01:05,874 --> 00:01:09,731
born of Dashrath's first queen, Kaushalya.

13
00:01:12,772 --> 00:01:15,924
Whenever there have been crises on the
earth Lord Vishnu

14
00:01:15,924 --> 00:01:18,739
has descended from the heavens for its
salvation.

15
00:01:19,779 --> 00:01:26,748
Lord Vishnu has ten incarnations and Ram
is believed to be his seventh incarnation.

16
00:01:28,788 --> 00:01:33,754
When Ram turned fifteen Ravan was at the
peak of his powers.

17
00:01:34,794 --> 00:01:39,117
Ravan's relation, Marich along with his
mother Tadaka

18
00:01:39,117 --> 00:01:43,602
was a terror for sage Vishwamitra and
other hermits who

19
00:01:43,602 --> 00:01:47,354
lived in a forest close to Ayodhya's
border.

20
00:01:48,613 --> 00:01:51,535
They disturbed Vishwamitra's prayers,
every day.

21
00:01:52,621 --> 00:01:54,676
And on one such day...

22
00:03:03,875 --> 00:03:09,934
O Lord Vishnu is there no one who can save
us from this torment?

23
00:03:12,237 --> 00:03:14,114
His name is Ram.

24
00:03:15,200 --> 00:03:19,334
First born prince of King Dashrath, of
Ayodhya.

25
00:04:16,001 --> 00:04:21,013
O sage of sages, my court is indeed
blessed by your presence.

26
00:04:21,227 --> 00:04:23,104
What is it that you desire of me?

27
00:04:23,318 --> 00:04:25,194
Let me fulfill your command!

28
00:04:25,409 --> 00:04:31,132
O noble king of the Solar Dynasty the
demons ruined the sacred land and

29
00:04:31,132 --> 00:04:36,693
we are in great trouble. I need your
eldest son Ram to destroy them.

30
00:04:41,088 --> 00:04:44,010
Ram!? He is but a mere boy.

31
00:04:44,224 --> 00:04:47,146
I, myself, shall wipe them off from the
face of this earth.

32
00:04:47,360 --> 00:04:52,372
This is a command from the Gods O King, do
you dare reject it?

33
00:04:52,586 --> 00:04:56,553
Dashrath, send your sons Ram and Lakshman.

34
00:04:56,768 --> 00:05:01,785
Vishwamitra is strong and wise and has
mastery over every weapon.

35
00:05:01,994 --> 00:05:03,871
He will protect your sons.

36
00:05:07,221 --> 00:05:11,188
Ram... Lakshman come here, my sons!

37
00:05:15,583 --> 00:05:19,550
O sage Vishwamitra I leave my sons with
you.

38
00:05:19,764 --> 00:05:21,641
Give them guidance and courage.

39
00:05:21,855 --> 00:05:23,731
Bless you, King Dashrath!

40
00:05:23,945 --> 00:05:27,914
You have made a decision that shall save
the world.

41
00:05:28,301 --> 00:05:31,045
We will obey you like we obey our father.

42
00:05:31,262 --> 00:05:33,139
Your wishes will be our command.

43
00:06:02,448 --> 00:06:06,710
You know, once this was a beautiful forest
but now it has dried

44
00:06:06,710 --> 00:06:10,770
up because of a terrible cannibal a
demoness called Tadaka.

45
00:06:10,984 --> 00:06:17,042
Her son, the evil Marich leads the demons
who defile the holy fires.

46
00:06:17,256 --> 00:06:19,132
Ram, you must kill Tadaka.

47
00:06:19,346 --> 00:06:21,223
That is your dharma!

48
00:06:21,437 --> 00:06:23,313
Your duty as a Kshatriya!

49
00:06:24,399 --> 00:06:26,455
I shall teach you Mantras...

50
00:06:26,663 --> 00:06:28,540
They will guide you.

51
00:06:29,799 --> 00:06:31,676
Now... repeat after me.

52
00:06:49,487 --> 00:06:51,542
Stop it!

53
00:06:53,668 --> 00:06:57,802
That mantra tears apart...

54
00:07:28,163 --> 00:07:31,263
Ram, use the mantra. Recite the mantra!

55
00:08:15,375 --> 00:08:21,266
Ram, Lakshman. Many years ago in this very place, the
Gods rewarded my

56
00:08:21,266 --> 00:08:27,184
long years of penance with the mastery of
supreme weapons.

57
00:08:28,460 --> 00:08:34,599
The time has now come for me to pass on
these weapons to one worthy of them.

58
00:08:40,113 --> 00:08:43,074
Take them, Ram, and use them well.

59
00:08:52,648 --> 00:08:54,731
They are now yours.

60
00:08:54,942 --> 00:08:56,843
Use them to protect 'Dharma'.

61
00:09:16,128 --> 00:09:20,149
That's him! The one who killed my mother.

62
00:09:20,365 --> 00:09:24,385
I shall avenge her with his blood this I
swear!

63
00:09:27,604 --> 00:09:29,687
Watch out!

64
00:10:03,795 --> 00:10:05,697
You used the divine weapons!

65
00:10:05,914 --> 00:10:07,816
How did you learn so soon?

66
00:10:08,033 --> 00:10:09,934
These are the weapons of the Gods.

67
00:10:12,095 --> 00:10:15,236
And the righteous one needs no lessons to
use them.

68
00:10:16,507 --> 00:10:20,527
Show me, my Guru how to use this Chakra?

69
00:10:20,744 --> 00:10:25,824
You will learn but only if you pursue your
destiny in righteousness.

70
00:10:39,635 --> 00:10:41,717
Listen all!

71
00:10:41,929 --> 00:10:44,890
This is the great bow of Shiva!

72
00:10:45,107 --> 00:10:51,251
He who lifts it and strings it shall
receive a great reward from King Janak.

73
00:10:52,522 --> 00:10:58,661
The winner shall be given the hand of
Princess Sita. in marriage.

74
00:11:27,478 --> 00:11:30,439
Next, Prince Jagtara of Sorav.

75
00:11:50,254 --> 00:11:54,275
Next, the Prince Ram of Ayodhya.

76
00:12:51,692 --> 00:12:54,653
Congratulations on your wedding, Prince
Ram.

77
00:13:13,937 --> 00:13:15,838
Years passed.

78
00:13:16,055 --> 00:13:17,957
Ayodhya grew and prospered.

79
00:13:18,174 --> 00:13:20,075
And the people loved Ram.

80
00:13:21,175 --> 00:13:23,257
Their prince and king-to-be.

81
00:13:23,470 --> 00:13:28,550
The four brothers live in harmony and
their future looks full of hope.

82
00:13:31,945 --> 00:13:34,905
My people, this morning I awoke from a
dream full of omens.

83
00:13:35,123 --> 00:13:39,143
Guru Vashishtha sees in them the coming of
troubled times.

84
00:13:41,478 --> 00:13:43,380
But my health is failing...

85
00:13:43,597 --> 00:13:47,617
I am getting old and have no more power to
resist those evil forces.

86
00:13:48,716 --> 00:13:52,913
I have, therefore, decided that Ram will
succeed me.

87
00:13:54,189 --> 00:13:56,090
He will be the next king of Ayodhya.

88
00:13:56,308 --> 00:13:59,268
Ram, my son, come forward.

89
00:14:04,782 --> 00:14:07,743
Ram, try to live up to the people's
expectations.

90
00:14:07,960 --> 00:14:09,861
I have faith in you.

91
00:14:10,078 --> 00:14:14,099
I will do my utmost to live up to the
ideals you have set for us.

92
00:14:14,316 --> 00:14:16,217
Long live Ayodhya!

93
00:14:16,434 --> 00:14:18,336
Long live King Dashrath!

94
00:14:18,553 --> 00:14:20,454
Long live Prince Ram!

95
00:14:31,087 --> 00:14:33,170
Get away... get away.

96
00:14:33,382 --> 00:14:36,344
Noisy wretched things!

97
00:14:36,560 --> 00:14:38,463
Manthara, stop abusing the birds.

98
00:14:39,561 --> 00:14:43,758
Aah... Kekeyi, is this the time to
beautify yourself?

99
00:14:43,975 --> 00:14:46,936
When great misfortune creeps upon the
kingdom?

100
00:14:47,153 --> 00:14:50,114
Manthara, don't you understand?

101
00:14:54,392 --> 00:14:58,588
Our beloved Ram is to be anointed crown
prince tomorrow.

102
00:14:58,805 --> 00:15:01,766
And so I said, it is a misfortune.

103
00:15:01,983 --> 00:15:07,063
Oh Kekeyi you are so innocent!

104
00:15:07,280 --> 00:15:13,419
So trusting! And look look how King
Dashrath has betrayed your trust!?

105
00:15:13,636 --> 00:15:15,537
Hold your tongue, Manthara.

106
00:15:15,754 --> 00:15:17,656
I will never allow you to speak of the
King in this way.

107
00:15:17,873 --> 00:15:22,952
Why? Why do you think the king sent Bharat
away, now?

108
00:15:23,168 --> 00:15:28,249
So conveniently before the coronation!
Why!?

109
00:15:29,524 --> 00:15:32,485
Why? I wonder why he did that?

110
00:15:34,644 --> 00:15:39,900
Kaushalya might have suggested it to the
king. Yes!

111
00:15:40,117 --> 00:15:46,256
You know you are the king's favorite queen
and Kaushalya hates you for that.

112
00:15:46,473 --> 00:15:51,552
She is jealous... jealous of your youth
and beauty, aah!

113
00:15:52,829 --> 00:15:54,730
What can I do?

114
00:15:54,947 --> 00:16:00,027
Leave everything to this loyal and clever
Manthara.

115
00:16:24,607 --> 00:16:26,508
What's happened?

116
00:16:27,785 --> 00:16:31,805
Why this sorrow, this anger on such an
auspicious night?

117
00:16:32,022 --> 00:16:33,923
What can I do? Come, tell me.

118
00:16:34,140 --> 00:16:39,220
Tell me O King, do you remember when you
were injured in a battle some years ago?

119
00:16:47,911 --> 00:16:55,102
I drove you to safety and you promised to
fulfill two boons of mine.

120
00:16:59,564 --> 00:17:03,584
You must grant me those two boons, now!

121
00:17:03,800 --> 00:17:05,702
Only two boons!?

122
00:17:07,861 --> 00:17:09,943
You can have more, if you want.

123
00:17:10,156 --> 00:17:12,057
No, I don't need more than two.

124
00:17:13,157 --> 00:17:15,239
The first is...

125
00:17:17,394 --> 00:17:21,591
No... I cannot grant you those, Kekeyi.
Not those!

126
00:17:21,808 --> 00:17:24,769
I will give you all my wealth. Will that
please you? - No.

127
00:17:26,928 --> 00:17:32,184
Do you wanted to be known that a king of
Solar Dynasty went back on his words.

128
00:17:32,401 --> 00:17:37,480
I will be content with only those two
boons.

129
00:17:40,875 --> 00:17:47,804
The boons were one, Kekeyi's son, Bharat,
to be made king and two,

130
00:17:47,804 --> 00:17:53,370
Ram to be banished to the forest for
fourteen years.

131
00:17:55,528 --> 00:17:57,611
Brother, can you not hear the people's
voices?

132
00:17:57,823 --> 00:18:00,784
Lakshman, this is part of my fate.

133
00:18:01,001 --> 00:18:04,699
But are we, on that account to sit still
and do nothing?

134
00:18:04,699 --> 00:18:08,199
This sword is it only an ornament, just a
plaything?

135
00:18:08,416 --> 00:18:14,102
Brother, you are part of my self, sharing
the same soul with me.

136
00:18:14,102 --> 00:18:16,678
Please try to understand me.

137
00:18:16,891 --> 00:18:18,792
My Lord, I am coming with you.

138
00:18:20,598 --> 00:18:21,970
But Sita, you...

139
00:18:24,306 --> 00:18:27,267
A husband's duty is his wife's too.

140
00:18:27,484 --> 00:18:29,385
Your fate is equally mine. - That's right!

141
00:18:32,780 --> 00:18:34,682
And the same soul should follow the same
fate.

142
00:18:34,899 --> 00:18:37,860
And so brother, I, too, am coming with
you.

143
00:18:41,077 --> 00:18:43,160
Thank you!

144
00:18:53,789 --> 00:18:55,871
Mother... take heart!

145
00:18:56,084 --> 00:18:57,985
Fourteen years will pass very quickly.

146
00:18:58,202 --> 00:19:02,224
And I will be back, seeking your blessings
in no time at all.

147
00:19:02,440 --> 00:19:04,341
Yes, my son. - Ram!

148
00:19:14,974 --> 00:19:18,116
Ram, why don't you blame me?

149
00:19:18,329 --> 00:19:20,231
Why don't you bear a grudge against me?

150
00:19:20,448 --> 00:19:22,349
That would ease my guilt.

151
00:19:23,448 --> 00:19:26,591
I don't want the kingdom. Nor the power.

152
00:19:26,802 --> 00:19:30,825
All I want are your blessings before we
depart. Father!

153
00:19:32,982 --> 00:19:35,065
My son, bring glory to our great line of
kings.

154
00:19:35,277 --> 00:19:37,178
Come back safe.

155
00:19:40,573 --> 00:19:43,534
Who in the world can boast of a son like
you?

156
00:19:47,988 --> 00:19:52,199
Sumantra get ready the chariots, the
elephants,

157
00:19:52,199 --> 00:19:57,305
horses and foot soldiers to accompany Ram
to the forest.

158
00:19:57,522 --> 00:19:59,424
Yes, your majesty!

159
00:19:59,641 --> 00:20:03,031
Father, when nature herself will take care
of me what

160
00:20:03,031 --> 00:20:05,780
use I have of an army, of royal pageantry?

161
00:20:05,997 --> 00:20:12,135
Of course, you will give Bharat this
kingdom after draining it of all its
wealth.

162
00:20:32,478 --> 00:20:35,439
Mother, give your blessings to your
departing son.

163
00:20:46,073 --> 00:20:48,155
Ram, don't leave us.

164
00:20:48,368 --> 00:20:51,328
Remain as our king. - Beloved citizens...

165
00:20:52,427 --> 00:20:54,511
You know how much I love you.

166
00:20:54,723 --> 00:20:56,625
And I know how much you love me.

167
00:20:56,842 --> 00:21:00,264
You will show your love for me by loving
my noble brother,

168
00:21:00,264 --> 00:21:04,040
Bharat who is fully worthy of your love
and of being your king.

169
00:21:05,315 --> 00:21:09,669
Support him, I beg of you. Support my
sorrowful father.

170
00:21:09,669 --> 00:21:12,519
People of Ayodhya, I appeal to you.

171
00:21:13,613 --> 00:21:16,755
Rama... don't go, Rama, Please.

172
00:21:34,799 --> 00:21:36,882
Ram... come back soon!

173
00:21:43,450 --> 00:21:45,352
O my son!

174
00:21:46,628 --> 00:21:48,530
Ram!

175
00:21:49,700 --> 00:21:53,826
Take care Ram, Lakshman, Sita!

176
00:21:54,042 --> 00:21:55,945
You take care too.

177
00:21:56,161 --> 00:21:59,123
And please, look after my father.

178
00:21:59,339 --> 00:22:01,240
I will.

179
00:22:53,186 --> 00:22:55,268
RAM!!!

180
00:23:13,382 --> 00:23:15,394
Six months passed by.

181
00:23:15,607 --> 00:23:19,628
King Dashrath's palace is enveloped in
darkness.

182
00:23:19,845 --> 00:23:24,928
Ram forgive your father.

183
00:23:25,141 --> 00:23:27,043
Ram... Ram!

184
00:23:32,555 --> 00:23:36,577
He is free from the sufferings of this
world.

185
00:23:41,913 --> 00:23:47,451
Bharat, Kekeyi's son who was away in
Kekeya visiting his

186
00:23:47,451 --> 00:23:51,406
grandfather was called back to Ayodhya.

187
00:24:18,987 --> 00:24:21,070
Mother... mother! What is this? What has
happened?

188
00:24:22,165 --> 00:24:25,307
Oh Bharat, you have come at last.

189
00:24:25,519 --> 00:24:29,541
Tell me mother, is it true, father has
passed away?

190
00:24:30,639 --> 00:24:32,722
Oh God!

191
00:24:33,817 --> 00:24:35,899
Then it is true! - Yes.

192
00:24:36,112 --> 00:24:39,073
But he left us a great honor. - What is
it?

193
00:24:45,646 --> 00:24:48,607
What have you done, you depraved heartless
woman?

194
00:24:50,943 --> 00:24:53,903
What perverse tongue poisoned your mind?

195
00:24:54,120 --> 00:24:56,022
Brother, it is she.

196
00:24:56,239 --> 00:25:02,378
It is this evil wretch who has sown the
seed of madness in our mother's heart.

197
00:25:02,595 --> 00:25:06,615
Please please forgive me.

198
00:25:07,714 --> 00:25:14,030
I was only thinking of you two Kekeyi and
Bharat's... - Stop it.

199
00:25:14,246 --> 00:25:18,267
I will cleave your filthy brain in two. -
That's enough.

200
00:25:18,483 --> 00:25:21,444
Don't let her blood defile our father's
soul.

201
00:25:22,721 --> 00:25:27,800
You are no longer my mother let the world
know it.

202
00:25:28,900 --> 00:25:37,334
Please forgive me forgive your poor
mother, Bharat please, forgive me.

203
00:25:39,493 --> 00:25:41,575
Forgive me!

204
00:25:50,156 --> 00:25:51,107
What?

205
00:25:52,204 --> 00:25:54,287
What are you saying, Bharat?

206
00:25:54,500 --> 00:25:57,460
Our father is dead!?

207
00:25:57,678 --> 00:26:01,698
Brother I share your grief.

208
00:26:09,329 --> 00:26:16,527
Father... father forgive this poor Ram
forgive your son, please.

209
00:26:17,803 --> 00:26:21,823
Ram, I appeal to you absolve me of my
mother's sin.

210
00:26:22,040 --> 00:26:26,427
Come back to Ayodhya and accept the
kingdom which is yours by right.

211
00:26:26,427 --> 00:26:30,298
- Bharat what your mother has done is not
in question here.

212
00:26:30,515 --> 00:26:35,867
Remember, the great Emperor Dashrath has
commanded us you to rule

213
00:26:35,867 --> 00:26:40,891
the kingdom and I to live in this forest
for fourteen years.

214
00:26:41,108 --> 00:26:46,187
It is our duty to abide by our father's
wishes whether we like it or not.

215
00:26:46,404 --> 00:26:48,306
You have commanded me, it is enough.

216
00:26:48,522 --> 00:26:50,425
But one thing is certain.

217
00:26:50,641 --> 00:26:53,602
I will not accept the kingdom for myself.

218
00:26:53,818 --> 00:26:55,720
But for you!

219
00:26:59,115 --> 00:27:04,232
Please bless this brother of yours to rule
the kingdom with strength and courage.

220
00:27:15,103 --> 00:27:19,147
I will rule for the next fourteen years
but only till you return.

221
00:27:19,364 --> 00:27:22,876
Bharat, my brother. - Ram.

222
00:27:23,094 --> 00:27:25,187
Long live Ram.

223
00:27:25,402 --> 00:27:27,665
Long live Bharat.

224
00:28:33,762 --> 00:28:37,984
What brings my chief minister out here at
this unlikely hour?

225
00:28:38,202 --> 00:28:41,541
Sir, in the forest of Dandaka and
Janasthana they say

226
00:28:41,541 --> 00:28:44,376
the holy men are returning to their
ashrams.

227
00:28:44,594 --> 00:28:46,506
They seem to have gained a new confidence.

228
00:28:46,724 --> 00:28:51,834
Our spies say, it is the doing of the
young prince of Ayodhya, Prince Ram.

229
00:28:54,004 --> 00:28:58,218
Oh, this boy Ram is handsome, isn't he?

230
00:28:59,332 --> 00:29:04,617
I've heard this Ram is a cowards who has
been sent into exile by his own people.

231
00:29:04,836 --> 00:29:08,880
That's right, my king, but we must do
something before it is too late.

232
00:29:10,163 --> 00:29:14,207
Oh Ram, I can't wait to see you.

233
00:31:58,668 --> 00:32:00,580
Shurpankha, Ravan's younger sister...

234
00:32:00,798 --> 00:32:06,973
.disguised as a beautiful lady comes to
Panchvati to entice Ram.

235
00:32:08,256 --> 00:32:11,234
I am Shurpankha.

236
00:32:16,601 --> 00:32:21,892
Ram, you are so beautiful strong and
handsome.

237
00:32:22,105 --> 00:32:24,019
I have decided to marry you.

238
00:32:26,367 --> 00:32:30,410
Your wish would be my command were it not
for my wife Sita, there.

239
00:32:30,629 --> 00:32:33,606
Why don't you approach my brother,
Lakshman?

240
00:32:33,825 --> 00:32:36,802
He is also very handsome and very strong.

241
00:32:37,021 --> 00:32:39,999
Hmm... he is handsome too.

242
00:32:40,216 --> 00:32:43,195
I speak with your interest at heart. I am
only second to Ram.

243
00:32:43,413 --> 00:32:47,457
And I don't think you are the kind to
settle for second best!?

244
00:32:47,675 --> 00:32:49,587
Yes, you are right!

245
00:32:50,693 --> 00:32:53,852
I am the kind to settle only for the very
best.

246
00:32:54,954 --> 00:32:59,168
Come... come. I will introduce you to...
this is my wife Sita.

247
00:33:05,786 --> 00:33:11,960
This ugly one is your wife!? I will kill
her.

248
00:33:18,570 --> 00:33:20,483
Oh... my nose.

249
00:33:21,766 --> 00:33:23,679
My nose!!

250
00:33:24,785 --> 00:33:26,879
Bleeding!

251
00:33:29,046 --> 00:33:34,996
O the Energy which bestows knowledge to
conquer the phenomenon of death...

252
00:33:34,996 --> 00:33:39,660
may please rise... rise and bestow your
blessings! Swaha!

253
00:33:42,896 --> 00:33:44,990
Brother! - What's happened to you?

254
00:33:45,204 --> 00:33:48,182
O our little sister! What has happened!?

255
00:33:51,418 --> 00:33:54,579
Ram!? You mean that... that... prince from
Ayodhya!?

256
00:33:54,793 --> 00:33:57,770
Is he the one who attacked you?

257
00:34:12,904 --> 00:34:14,816
Do not worry, little sister.

258
00:34:15,034 --> 00:34:20,143
I will have these worms sliced up and and
feed the ravens for breakfast.

259
00:34:20,361 --> 00:34:22,273
Where is my brother Kumbhakarna?

260
00:34:22,492 --> 00:34:25,469
Tell him, I have said, he must lead the
attack.

261
00:34:48,061 --> 00:34:51,275
Just as I feared, my King your brother
Kumbhakarna won't

262
00:34:51,275 --> 00:34:53,169
wake up for the next six months.

263
00:34:53,387 --> 00:34:57,431
That Sita... I wish I could destroy her
beauty.

264
00:34:58,537 --> 00:35:00,630
Is she... that beautiful?

265
00:35:01,732 --> 00:35:05,946
There is no one more beautiful than her in
this whole world.

266
00:35:09,368 --> 00:35:17,673
Her waist is slim, her figure captivating
her complexion like molten gold.

267
00:35:20,021 --> 00:35:25,131
A heavenly maid who is designed for you,
my brother.

268
00:35:25,349 --> 00:35:27,261
She is not worthy of that Ram.

269
00:35:28,544 --> 00:35:31,522
There surely is someone who is worthy of
her.

270
00:35:31,740 --> 00:35:34,718
And that someone is you.

271
00:36:07,785 --> 00:36:13,071
Ravan, accompanied by his uncle Marich
sets out to kidnap Sita.

272
00:36:14,355 --> 00:36:17,333
Then... as we planned?

273
00:36:17,550 --> 00:36:21,595
Yes, as we planned!

274
00:36:26,962 --> 00:36:29,056
This is magnificent!!!

275
00:36:30,158 --> 00:36:33,318
And this can surely deceive Ram.

276
00:36:46,138 --> 00:36:48,232
Oh... how beautiful she is!

277
00:36:54,839 --> 00:36:57,817
Oh! How lovely!

278
00:36:58,035 --> 00:37:01,013
It 'is' real, isn't it? It's not a dream,
is it?

279
00:37:01,231 --> 00:37:04,209
O Ram, won't you capture the deer for me?

280
00:37:04,427 --> 00:37:07,404
It is the most beautiful thing I've ever
seen.

281
00:37:07,623 --> 00:37:10,601
For you? I will! Lakshman, look after
Sita.

282
00:37:18,277 --> 00:37:21,254
Brother, remember that this deer's beauty
is Shurpankha.

283
00:37:21,473 --> 00:37:24,450
Watch out! Watch out for those treacherous
creatures.

284
00:37:24,669 --> 00:37:26,581
All right! Protect Sita.

285
00:37:37,453 --> 00:37:40,431
So, it is a demon, disguised as a deer!

286
00:37:50,238 --> 00:37:54,282
You might be relieved that you have killed
me.

287
00:37:54,499 --> 00:37:57,477
But you better be worried about your
pretty wife.

288
00:37:57,695 --> 00:38:02,803
What? - Lakshman, Sita help me!

289
00:38:05,152 --> 00:38:08,131
Lakshman, did you hear that dreadful cry?

290
00:38:08,349 --> 00:38:11,327
Ram is in danger. He needs your help.

291
00:38:11,545 --> 00:38:14,523
O he will be safe. Don't worry, sister.

292
00:38:14,741 --> 00:38:17,719
What are you saying? You wish him dead?

293
00:38:19,002 --> 00:38:21,980
I understand, so, I will obey you!

294
00:38:34,983 --> 00:38:37,960
Sister, do not step outside this line.

295
00:38:38,179 --> 00:38:41,156
Within this line you are safe. I assure
you.

296
00:38:49,898 --> 00:38:53,942
Everything goes just as I planned.

297
00:39:18,485 --> 00:39:21,645
Om Namah Shivay! (Obeisance to Lord
Shiva!)

298
00:39:23,990 --> 00:39:29,102
O virtuous lady I come begging for alms.

299
00:39:45,297 --> 00:39:47,209
Here you are.

300
00:39:50,623 --> 00:39:52,536
Oh, I am surprised.

301
00:39:52,754 --> 00:39:55,733
Somebody has drawn it to protect you.

302
00:39:55,950 --> 00:39:58,928
I cannot cross it but you surely can.
Come.

303
00:40:00,034 --> 00:40:02,129
No... no.

304
00:40:02,343 --> 00:40:08,267
If you do not feed this hungry saint with
your hands then ruin shall

305
00:40:08,267 --> 00:40:13,844
fall upon your father's and
father-in-law's house O noble lady!

306
00:40:42,649 --> 00:40:45,808
Lakshman!? - Ram! - Why did you leave Sita
alone?

307
00:40:46,022 --> 00:40:49,001
Why are you here? - She insisted I leave
when we heard your cry.

308
00:40:49,218 --> 00:40:53,263
Oh no! That was the voice of demon
imitating mine.

309
00:40:53,480 --> 00:40:57,523
I fear the worst. Come let's get back as
soon as we can.

310
00:40:59,695 --> 00:41:01,789
Ram... Ram!

311
00:41:07,329 --> 00:41:09,243
Rescue me!

312
00:41:13,544 --> 00:41:16,704
Lakshman... Ram... help me!

313
00:41:17,806 --> 00:41:18,834
Sita!

314
00:41:20,114 --> 00:41:25,224
You are mine now. - No... no... Jatayu,
help me. No!!

315
00:41:33,964 --> 00:41:36,941
Let her go. She does not belong to you.

316
00:41:46,748 --> 00:41:48,661
Let me go. Oh!

317
00:41:55,271 --> 00:41:57,183
Jatayu...

318
00:42:06,812 --> 00:42:07,841
Will teach him a lesson.

319
00:42:11,074 --> 00:42:13,168
Jatayu...

320
00:42:16,578 --> 00:42:18,490
Let me go.

321
00:42:18,709 --> 00:42:21,687
No one can save you now.

322
00:42:35,577 --> 00:42:37,672
He tricked me!

323
00:42:37,885 --> 00:42:40,864
He tricked me and abducted my wife during
my absence.

324
00:42:43,213 --> 00:42:46,190
I swear, Lakshman, I swear. I shall try to
vanquish him.

325
00:42:47,296 --> 00:42:50,456
I shall follow that fellow into the ends
of the universe.

326
00:42:50,670 --> 00:42:52,582
I will seek him out.

327
00:42:52,800 --> 00:42:55,779
And I... will destroy him.

328
00:42:58,128 --> 00:43:01,617
Calm down, my brother Ram. You have always
said that

329
00:43:01,617 --> 00:43:04,301
anger is not the right path to justice.

330
00:43:04,520 --> 00:43:08,308
You, who have only the good of the world
at heart must

331
00:43:08,308 --> 00:43:10,693
not let anger plunge you into it.

332
00:43:12,865 --> 00:43:14,960
You are right... you are right, Lakshman.

333
00:43:16,061 --> 00:43:22,413
Now, it is your turn to lead my little
brother and I will follow.

334
00:43:23,519 --> 00:43:27,739
Lakshman, is this gentle creature trying
to tell us something about Sita?

335
00:43:27,957 --> 00:43:33,067
It might be showing us the direction in
which Sita has been taken. Let's go.

336
00:43:33,284 --> 00:43:37,329
Help me! Ram... Ram!!!

337
00:43:41,807 --> 00:43:43,720
Hey, what is this?

338
00:43:47,134 --> 00:43:52,243
Forgive me, Ram I tried to stop him, but
he cantered away.

339
00:43:52,460 --> 00:43:55,439
My old wings were too frail.

340
00:43:55,657 --> 00:44:00,765
Oh Jatayu how can I blame you?

341
00:44:01,872 --> 00:44:05,031
You have given your life's blood for my
beloved wife!

342
00:44:05,245 --> 00:44:09,459
Do not lose heart, Ram. You will find her
again.

343
00:44:09,664 --> 00:44:12,475
Jatayu... Jatayu...

344
00:44:18,714 --> 00:44:20,519
Where are you taking me?

345
00:44:21,563 --> 00:44:23,540
Let me go.

346
00:44:37,819 --> 00:44:42,008
Remember all of you. If anyone tries to
harm her, they will die.

347
00:44:42,008 --> 00:44:46,664
This is Lanka's future queen, take extra
care of her. 

348
00:44:47,708 --> 00:44:49,685
Trijata!? - What does Your Majesty wish of
me?

349
00:44:49,886 --> 00:44:51,691
I appoint you her keeper.

350
00:44:51,898 --> 00:44:55,226
Whatever she asks for in the Ashok Van see
that she gets it.

351
00:44:55,226 --> 00:44:56,724
- Very well, your Majesty.

352
00:44:56,925 --> 00:45:00,743
She is stubborn. But you must give her
everything she wants.

353
00:45:00,947 --> 00:45:02,753
Except freedom!

354
00:45:18,947 --> 00:45:24,876
Could it be human blood? Yum... yum...
yum.

355
00:45:25,081 --> 00:45:26,887
So good!

356
00:45:29,941 --> 00:45:31,918
An arrow!? Painful if it hits me.

357
00:45:33,963 --> 00:45:35,940
But it doesn't hit me.

358
00:45:41,002 --> 00:45:42,979
I got her!

359
00:46:15,359 --> 00:46:20,558
Thank you! I was a heavenly creature,
cursed to be an ugly demon.

360
00:46:20,558 --> 00:46:23,198
And no one could lift the curse.

361
00:46:23,403 --> 00:46:27,252
Only if I were defeated by a man of
justice I could regain

362
00:46:27,252 --> 00:46:30,238
my original self and go back to the
heavens.

363
00:46:31,280 --> 00:46:36,371
Thank you, Ram. But there is nothing I can
do for you in return,

364
00:46:36,371 --> 00:46:38,281
except give you advice.

365
00:46:38,487 --> 00:46:41,297
Find Sugriva now.

366
00:46:42,341 --> 00:46:44,318
Sugriva!? Who is he?

367
00:46:49,548 --> 00:46:51,353
It's a lake.

368
00:46:52,397 --> 00:46:54,374
Lakshman, now what do we do?

369
00:46:54,576 --> 00:46:57,287
There seems to be someone over there.
Let's go and ask

370
00:46:57,287 --> 00:46:59,397
them about Sugriva. - That's a good idea.

371
00:47:03,626 --> 00:47:05,431
Wait!

372
00:47:15,692 --> 00:47:21,520
And in the great mother's magic play all
of us perform our little roles.

373
00:47:23,738 --> 00:47:27,905
I never thought I could see a man of
knowledge like you in this wilderness.

374
00:47:27,905 --> 00:47:30,571
My name is Ram and this is my brother
Lakshman.

375
00:47:30,776 --> 00:47:32,581
We are the sons of King Dashrath of
Ayodhya.

376
00:47:32,787 --> 00:47:37,186
We come in search of my beloved wife, Sita
who has been

377
00:47:37,186 --> 00:47:40,625
carried away by a demon I know not, where?

378
00:47:40,832 --> 00:47:45,654
Indeed it is a benevolent destiny that
leads me to Prince Ram of Ayodhya.

379
00:47:47,703 --> 00:47:50,685
My name is Hanuman.

380
00:47:50,888 --> 00:47:53,698
And I am minister to the King Sugriva.

381
00:47:53,904 --> 00:47:57,808
Lakshman, we've been wondering where to
find Sugriva and

382
00:47:57,808 --> 00:48:00,737
here is Sugriva's messenger welcoming us.

383
00:48:00,944 --> 00:48:03,754
Indeed kind destiny has guided us here.

384
00:48:04,797 --> 00:48:08,616
Ram... Lakshman it is indeed an honor to
meet the sons of King

385
00:48:08,616 --> 00:48:12,804
Dashrath whose greatness is known in all
four corners of the world.

386
00:48:13,010 --> 00:48:18,838
Under strange circumstances I heard your
name called out Ram!

387
00:48:19,043 --> 00:48:23,056
Not many days ago, a flying chariot, swift
as a wind raced above

388
00:48:23,056 --> 00:48:26,882
our heads and we heard and we heard a
lady's cry for help...

389
00:48:27,088 --> 00:48:29,899
Ram... she cried. Help me Ram!

390
00:48:30,104 --> 00:48:32,915
From the chariot, a small bundle dropped
to the ground.

391
00:48:33,121 --> 00:48:36,938
We've kept it very carefully. - Where is
it? Where is it?

392
00:48:40,160 --> 00:48:47,998
Oh brother, look indeed they are her scarf
and the ornaments in her hair.

393
00:48:48,204 --> 00:48:52,022
Oh Sita... my Sita.

394
00:48:52,226 --> 00:48:56,044
Courage brother, Ram.

395
00:48:56,249 --> 00:48:58,054
You have no time to grieve. You must act
without delay.

396
00:48:58,260 --> 00:49:02,077
I have sworn to rescue Sita wherever she
may be.

397
00:49:03,120 --> 00:49:08,110
Hmm, do well I know how it hurts to be
without one's consort.

398
00:49:08,316 --> 00:49:13,137
My brother Bali, banished me from my
kingdom then used up my wife.

399
00:49:13,344 --> 00:49:17,908
Oh, if only I had the kingdom's army at my
disposal I would send

400
00:49:17,908 --> 00:49:22,188
my men to search the whole world to rescue
your wife, Sita.

401
00:49:22,393 --> 00:49:25,204
Look, let us make this government, O
Prince of Ayodhya...

402
00:49:25,410 --> 00:49:28,451
Let us forge our strength in friendship
and swear to relieve

403
00:49:28,451 --> 00:49:31,238
the sorrows that have befallen us both. -
Yes, let us.

404
00:49:32,282 --> 00:49:36,747
For the sake of a friend a man should be
ready to give

405
00:49:36,747 --> 00:49:41,294
up his wealth and comforts and if need be
life itself.

406
00:49:41,499 --> 00:49:46,321
I will live by this Dharm and help Ram in
every way.

407
00:49:46,527 --> 00:49:49,338
I swear it. - I swear it too.

408
00:49:50,549 --> 00:49:54,366
Ram fulfilled the promise given to Sugriva
and forked the mighty Bali.

409
00:49:55,577 --> 00:49:59,395
Bali was defeated and Sugriva regained his
wife and his kingdom.

410
00:49:59,599 --> 00:50:02,768
The monsoon clouds gathered like a herd of
elephants and

411
00:50:02,768 --> 00:50:05,427
reclaimed the Rishyamukha hills for many
days.

412
00:50:13,677 --> 00:50:17,066
And when the rain ceased and the sun shone
again Rishyamukha

413
00:50:17,066 --> 00:50:20,511
stood like an island. surrounded by the
waters of the flood.

414
00:50:23,733 --> 00:50:26,544
And Sugriva called forth his great army of
monkeys.

415
00:50:26,750 --> 00:50:29,643
When you find my Sita, give her these
ornaments so she

416
00:50:29,643 --> 00:50:31,571
may recognize you as my emissaries.

417
00:50:51,888 --> 00:50:55,706
These are the jewels of my clan. Please
give them to her.

418
00:51:05,799 --> 00:51:08,602
The vanara king Sugriva sent search
parties in all

419
00:51:08,602 --> 00:51:10,789
directions keeping his promise to Ram.

420
00:51:32,111 --> 00:51:33,916
Help... it's a tiger. Help!

421
00:51:48,032 --> 00:51:50,009
Look... look... over there.

422
00:51:50,211 --> 00:51:53,022
If a bird came out of that cave, there
might be some water inside.

423
00:51:53,228 --> 00:51:56,039
Yes, perhaps we will find some water
there.

424
00:52:17,194 --> 00:52:19,170
They have gone inside. - Gone inside now.

425
00:52:36,467 --> 00:52:38,272
Hey, I can see some light.

426
00:52:40,489 --> 00:52:42,294
That must be the way out. C'mon.

427
00:52:47,528 --> 00:52:52,637
Hanuman, who leads the party to the south
meets Sampaati

428
00:52:52,637 --> 00:52:58,384
brother of Jatayu the bird king, killed at
the hands of Ravan.

429
00:52:58,589 --> 00:53:00,395
Where are we?

430
00:53:07,640 --> 00:53:12,462
Are you not Jatayu's brother, Sampaati!?

431
00:53:17,695 --> 00:53:21,513
Yes, I am Sampaati.

432
00:53:21,717 --> 00:53:24,529
Do you know my brother?

433
00:53:24,734 --> 00:53:27,544
How is my Jatayu?

434
00:53:28,588 --> 00:53:30,565
Is he well?

435
00:53:30,768 --> 00:53:33,578
Jatayu has found a home in the heavens.

436
00:53:38,812 --> 00:53:40,617
Oh... how sad!

437
00:53:41,661 --> 00:53:43,638
How sad!

438
00:53:44,677 --> 00:53:52,685
My brother to die and I live on.

439
00:53:52,890 --> 00:53:59,662
Old though he was he fought a difficult
battle with an evil demon,

440
00:53:59,662 --> 00:54:07,768
Ravan and was slain as he tried to save
Mother Sita from the demon's clutches?

441
00:54:07,973 --> 00:54:11,790
You said Ravan!? Ravan is the name!?

442
00:54:11,996 --> 00:54:16,561
If I knew he had killed my brother I would
never have

443
00:54:16,561 --> 00:54:19,834
let him fly over this land, unharmed.

444
00:54:20,878 --> 00:54:22,854
He flew over here?

445
00:54:23,057 --> 00:54:30,895
Yes, look across the sea is Lanka.

446
00:54:31,939 --> 00:54:39,939
There you will find and his captive the
lady.

447
00:54:40,152 --> 00:54:44,973
If we cross the sea with all the troops we
will need thousands of boats.

448
00:54:46,017 --> 00:54:48,999
And I am too old now.

449
00:54:49,201 --> 00:54:53,018
Though in my youth I had circled the earth
21 times.

450
00:54:56,073 --> 00:55:00,056
Now, there is only one among us who can
handle this task.

451
00:55:01,100 --> 00:55:06,368
When you were a boy believing the new born
sun to be a golden

452
00:55:06,368 --> 00:55:11,118
fruit you once flew after it meaning to
swallow it up.

453
00:55:11,324 --> 00:55:17,152
You had great powers but you did not know
how to use them.

454
00:55:18,195 --> 00:55:23,315
The world was afraid of you and so you
were put under a

455
00:55:23,315 --> 00:55:26,201
spell that sealed your powers.

456
00:55:26,407 --> 00:55:31,229
But the time has not come for me to unseal
these hidden powers.

457
00:55:32,272 --> 00:55:36,250
Only you can cross the sea with your
divine powers.

458
00:55:36,463 --> 00:55:40,280
Only you can reach Lanka and find mother
Sita.

459
00:56:24,562 --> 00:56:26,538
I... can fly!

460
00:56:32,606 --> 00:56:35,589
He has done it... he has done it! How
wonderful!

461
00:56:39,814 --> 00:56:43,630
Farewell prince!

462
00:56:50,706 --> 00:56:55,696
Hanuman rushes towards Lanka but is
challenged by the sea monster Sindhika.

463
00:56:56,740 --> 00:56:58,717
What's that?

464
00:57:34,951 --> 00:57:36,928
Where am I?

465
00:57:38,136 --> 00:57:39,941
I must get out of here.

466
00:57:59,253 --> 00:58:03,070
Now I will cut you up to little pieces.

467
00:58:04,113 --> 00:58:09,879
After a furious battle Hanuman tears the
monster to pieces

468
00:58:09,879 --> 00:58:12,749
and proceeds towards the island of Lanka.

469
01:00:03,713 --> 01:00:06,625
But on earth do I find Sita?

470
01:00:41,179 --> 01:00:42,942
Ah... you are awake.

471
01:00:43,961 --> 01:00:47,843
My day begins only when I see the radiance
of your face.

472
01:00:48,051 --> 01:00:50,795
And were you... you won't even look at me.

473
01:00:50,996 --> 01:00:52,758
Do you not see I am starving for your
love?

474
01:00:53,941 --> 01:00:56,685
Perhaps I should make a gift of Ram's
head.

475
01:00:56,886 --> 01:00:58,648
So, you have visited her again.

476
01:00:58,849 --> 01:01:00,611
Leave her alone, my Lord.

477
01:01:00,812 --> 01:01:03,556
Let's sing and dance over there. Let's
make merry.

478
01:01:06,538 --> 01:01:09,451
There is only a little time left. The
promise, dear, will soon be over.

479
01:01:16,519 --> 01:01:19,263
Huh! How on earth is our lord attracted by
you?

480
01:01:19,464 --> 01:01:22,207
I wonder what he sees in you!?

481
01:01:22,409 --> 01:01:25,798
I would like to see your husband. I can't
imagine anyone

482
01:01:25,798 --> 01:01:28,097
more handsome than the Lord of Lanka.

483
01:01:28,298 --> 01:01:32,024
Go away all of you. Do not annoy Sita or I
will have to answer to Ravan.

484
01:01:42,042 --> 01:01:47,735
O Ram! Ram, my husband come to save me
quickly.

485
01:01:48,750 --> 01:01:50,680
O Ram!

486
01:01:51,695 --> 01:01:55,577
O mother, I am the emissary of Ram.

487
01:01:56,602 --> 01:02:00,485
O mother, I am the emissary of Ram.

488
01:02:01,511 --> 01:02:10,310
I bow at your feet having this great
opportunity with me.

489
01:02:10,510 --> 01:02:14,236
O mother, I am the emissary of Ram.

490
01:02:14,436 --> 01:02:19,144
O mother, I am Ram's emissary.

491
01:02:29,979 --> 01:02:35,122
The radiance of my Lord is like the
shining sun and his

492
01:02:35,122 --> 01:02:38,769
voice is as soothing as the moonlight.

493
01:02:39,795 --> 01:02:46,630
You have been abducted by Ravan and he has
called for his own death by doing so.

494
01:02:46,831 --> 01:02:51,539
O mother, I am the emissary of Ram.

495
01:02:51,739 --> 01:02:56,448
O mother, I am the emissary of Ram.

496
01:03:07,281 --> 01:03:11,164
My Lord remains deep in thought, each
moment.

497
01:03:11,372 --> 01:03:15,099
But he constantly thinks about you only.

498
01:03:16,117 --> 01:03:22,951
His eyes are always longing to see you,
that's my own knowledge.

499
01:03:23,152 --> 01:03:27,860
O mother, I am the emissary of Ram.

500
01:03:28,060 --> 01:03:32,768
O mother, I am the emissary of Ram.

501
01:03:43,767 --> 01:03:47,493
Come with me, mother. I will take you back
to Ram.

502
01:03:47,693 --> 01:03:50,919
I can't go with you. There are many people
in Lanka who

503
01:03:50,919 --> 01:03:53,383
have been abducted and enslaved by force.

504
01:03:53,583 --> 01:03:56,327
I'm not the only one who is to be rescued.

505
01:03:57,346 --> 01:03:59,276
Hmm... I understand. I am leaving now.

506
01:03:59,473 --> 01:04:05,162
But soon your beloved husband Ram will
defeat Ravan and release the people of
Lanka.

507
01:04:05,363 --> 01:04:09,089
Take heart, be courageous, till the day of
liberty comes.

508
01:04:09,289 --> 01:04:12,033
Tell Ram to come and save me quickly.

509
01:04:12,234 --> 01:04:14,979
I will be hopeful till then. - I will
surely tell him.

510
01:04:16,979 --> 01:04:20,862
Before I leave, I must teach Ravan and his
friends a lesson.

511
01:04:23,850 --> 01:04:26,762
Besides, I need the exercise.

512
01:04:38,576 --> 01:04:39,524
Douse the fire.

513
01:04:45,447 --> 01:04:47,377
The next one promises to be a better match
for me.

514
01:04:57,227 --> 01:05:01,323
Perhaps, if I let myself to be captured I
will be able

515
01:05:01,323 --> 01:05:04,055
to see Ravan himself, face to face.

516
01:05:05,080 --> 01:05:07,010
Help! I can't stand the fire.

517
01:05:10,970 --> 01:05:16,822
You there!? What is your name and who has
sent you to Lanka?

518
01:05:22,913 --> 01:05:25,657
O Lord of Lanka, I am Hanuman.

519
01:05:25,858 --> 01:05:30,285
I come to you with respect as a messenger
of Lord Sugriva the

520
01:05:30,285 --> 01:05:34,494
Vanara King and devoted friend of Ram,
Prince of Ayodhya.

521
01:05:34,694 --> 01:05:38,420
You know it was a cowardly act to carry
off Princess Sita.

522
01:05:38,620 --> 01:05:40,382
Totally contrary to Dharm.

523
01:05:41,401 --> 01:05:45,291
This will surely end in your destruction
and the destruction of your race.

524
01:05:47,291 --> 01:05:51,174
Restore Sita to the prince and seek his
forgiveness.

525
01:05:53,181 --> 01:05:55,111
Kill him.

526
01:05:57,108 --> 01:05:59,206
According to the law of kings, you may
mutilate,

527
01:05:59,206 --> 01:06:00,997
brand or whip a messenger, but kill him?

528
01:06:01,198 --> 01:06:04,925
Why? What's wrong in killing a creature
such as this?

529
01:06:05,125 --> 01:06:09,832
If you slay him, what chance is there of
our real enemies being brought here?

530
01:06:11,015 --> 01:06:13,758
All right, but set fire to his tail first.
Then let him go home.

531
01:06:20,831 --> 01:06:23,575
Oh... it's hot. It's burning me. Help!

532
01:06:28,520 --> 01:06:33,395
It's hot... it's hot... it's hot it's
hot... it's hot... - Stop him! Stop him!

533
01:07:07,786 --> 01:07:10,698
Keep moving... keep moving, friends...
move forward.

534
01:07:11,713 --> 01:07:17,559
Victory awaits you! Friends, keep moving.

535
01:07:17,767 --> 01:07:25,421
With Ram's name on the lips, move ahead,
friends.

536
01:07:25,620 --> 01:07:31,309
Keep moving... keep moving, friends...
move forward.

537
01:07:35,437 --> 01:07:39,163
The ray of the sun is guiding our way.

538
01:07:40,181 --> 01:07:46,027
Gods believe that the demons should be
finished off.

539
01:07:48,034 --> 01:07:54,863
This is a war for the truth and removal of
the sins.

540
01:07:55,070 --> 01:08:01,742
The God of fire is with us, move ahead,
step-by-step.

541
01:08:01,941 --> 01:08:03,703
Keep moving, step-by-step.

542
01:08:05,704 --> 01:08:11,550
Keep moving... keep moving, friends...
move forward.

543
01:08:15,684 --> 01:08:19,411
The race of the demons is at the verge of
ruin.

544
01:08:19,611 --> 01:08:25,301
Finish off the evil with the blows of your
fists.

545
01:08:27,301 --> 01:08:30,212
This war is for justice.

546
01:08:31,391 --> 01:08:35,118
So be proud of yourself.

547
01:08:35,318 --> 01:08:42,972
With Ram's name on the lips, move ahead,
friends.

548
01:08:45,134 --> 01:08:50,824
Keep moving... keep moving friends... move
ahead.

549
01:09:05,585 --> 01:09:10,073
Ravan, my brother, I have come to beg you.
Return Sita to Ram or I fear the

550
01:09:10,073 --> 01:09:14,382
next time not only the city but the palace
itself will go up in flames.

551
01:09:15,401 --> 01:09:19,832
You spoke this. If anyone else had the
gall to speak to me like this,

552
01:09:19,832 --> 01:09:23,236
I might have killed him on the spot. I...
King Ravan,

553
01:09:23,236 --> 01:09:27,025
who has won the obedience of all men and
the praises of the

554
01:09:27,025 --> 01:09:31,071
Gods you expect me to shiver from fear of
a mere princeling?

555
01:09:31,271 --> 01:09:34,998
Be gone treacherous one. Get out. Get out
of my sight.

556
01:09:46,815 --> 01:09:49,609
Quiet! Quiet! How do we cross over to the
other side?

557
01:09:49,609 --> 01:09:52,667
- We will need thousands of boats for
these great troops.

558
01:09:53,686 --> 01:09:56,100
Then we can build a bridge. - A bridge!?
Do you know how

559
01:09:56,100 --> 01:09:58,556
many years it will take to construct such
a long bridge?

560
01:09:59,575 --> 01:10:02,528
If it is only mother Sita to be rescued, I
would fly to

561
01:10:02,528 --> 01:10:05,428
Lanka and accomplish the mission myself
quite easily.

562
01:10:05,630 --> 01:10:08,373
We have to rescue not only Sita but others
too.

563
01:10:08,575 --> 01:10:13,282
Ravan must be destroyed or else there will
be no lasting peace on earth.

564
01:10:16,263 --> 01:10:20,165
Listen all of you. A demon, named
Vibhishana a brother of Ravan,

565
01:10:20,165 --> 01:10:22,116
comes in peace, seeking refuge.

566
01:10:27,062 --> 01:10:30,944
He disagreed with his brother and
protected me in Ravan's palace.

567
01:10:31,152 --> 01:10:33,896
I have observed his honest nature for
myself.

568
01:10:34,097 --> 01:10:36,841
I see no fault in his joining our forces.

569
01:10:37,042 --> 01:10:39,787
I agree with Hanuman.

570
01:10:40,805 --> 01:10:42,736
You are now amongst friends.

571
01:10:42,932 --> 01:10:44,694
Bless me, O Lord.

572
01:10:45,713 --> 01:10:49,272
I have overheard your discussion on how to
cross over to Lanka.

573
01:10:49,272 --> 01:10:52,547
I'd like to suggest you pray to the Sea
God for His help.

574
01:10:52,749 --> 01:10:54,511
That's good advice, Vibhishana.

575
01:10:57,494 --> 01:11:03,346
For seven days and seven nights Ram prayed
to the Sea God.

576
01:11:08,292 --> 01:11:11,203
On the eighth dawn, the God revealed
Himself.

577
01:11:30,870 --> 01:11:35,733
Righteous Ram, build a bridge with stones.

578
01:11:35,942 --> 01:11:42,612
Inscribe your name on each stone and the
stones will not sink in the ocean.

579
01:11:42,813 --> 01:11:49,048
Instead they will support not only monkeys
but all the living creatures on

580
01:11:49,048 --> 01:11:55,366
the mountains<i>....</i> and in the seas
shall help you build this bridge.

581
01:11:55,574 --> 01:11:58,318
And the Gods shall bless you with success.

582
01:12:04,409 --> 01:12:08,136
Now... let's start! Let us build the
bridge.

583
01:12:09,154 --> 01:12:11,084
Hail! Hail!

584
01:12:11,281 --> 01:12:19,916
A bridge was built in the name of Ram.

585
01:12:20,933 --> 01:12:24,816
On the heart of the sea, across the
ocean...

586
01:12:25,842 --> 01:12:39,540
On the heart of the sea, across the ocean
a bridge was built in the name of Ram.

587
01:12:42,530 --> 01:12:51,321
All the stones and rocks were collected to
make the bridge.

588
01:12:51,529 --> 01:12:59,182
On the heart of the ocean they were
laid...

589
01:12:59,381 --> 01:13:05,595
On the heart of the ocean they were laid
with the blessings of the

590
01:13:05,595 --> 01:13:11,903
feet of Raghupati (Ram) with the blessings
of the feet of Raghupati

591
01:13:11,903 --> 01:13:17,833
and by his mere touch the stones started
floating in the sea.

592
01:13:18,851 --> 01:13:27,642
A bridge was built in the name of Ram.

593
01:13:33,576 --> 01:13:40,468
Just as the stones kept floating so does
the name of Ram,

594
01:13:40,468 --> 01:13:44,338
floats one in this sea of life.

595
01:13:45,356 --> 01:13:52,560
A remembrance of the glorious tale of Ram
a remembrance of the glorious

596
01:13:52,560 --> 01:13:59,055
tale of Ram is sufficient to give success
in all the endeavors.

597
01:13:59,262 --> 01:14:03,971
Devotion towards Ram is the key to
success.

598
01:14:04,171 --> 01:14:08,879
Just the name of Ram is enough to settle
all matters.

599
01:14:09,897 --> 01:14:17,714
A bridge was built in the name of Ram.

600
01:14:18,896 --> 01:14:27,523
On the heart of the sea, across the ocean,
a bridge was built in the name of Ram.

601
01:14:32,639 --> 01:14:38,328
Members of the council, we are facing an
outbreak of war.

602
01:14:38,529 --> 01:14:40,291
What do you have to say, Prahastha?

603
01:14:41,310 --> 01:14:45,351
Your Majesty, you as the great lord of
Lanka need not

604
01:14:45,351 --> 01:14:50,308
have called this council just to consider
this ridiculous threat,

605
01:14:50,308 --> 01:14:53,053
from a handful of men and monkeys.

606
01:14:54,071 --> 01:14:58,512
Just send a couple of my men who are not
even present in

607
01:14:58,512 --> 01:15:02,873
this council and they will surely wipe out
Ram's army.

608
01:15:03,070 --> 01:15:07,780
Ravan I told you before but now I have to
repeat it.

609
01:15:07,780 --> 01:15:13,668
Those who govern the kingdom should never
be swayed by flattery.

610
01:15:14,686 --> 01:15:17,597
The armies attacking us are no ordinary
ones.

611
01:15:18,612 --> 01:15:21,525
Ravan, I will tell you this for your own
good.

612
01:15:22,540 --> 01:15:25,451
Return Sita, she is the wife of the Prince
of Ayodhya.

613
01:15:25,648 --> 01:15:30,027
Grandfather why do we have to return her
now?

614
01:15:30,027 --> 01:15:37,227
If we release her now they will think that
we are all afraid of fighting.

615
01:15:38,245 --> 01:15:43,404
That is not so!? I cannot bear the sight
of so many people

616
01:15:43,404 --> 01:15:48,029
injured and even more dead just for this
one woman.

617
01:15:48,226 --> 01:15:51,953
Grandfather, that means you are afraid of
fighting.

618
01:15:52,971 --> 01:15:55,882
If you are scared of bloodshed how can you
fight?

619
01:15:56,079 --> 01:15:59,806
Indrajeet, I am no coward.

620
01:16:00,006 --> 01:16:03,732
But yes, I don't want to fight
unnecessarily.

621
01:16:05,732 --> 01:16:10,496
You called me, O Ram. - Yes, brave Prince
of the Vanaras please,

622
01:16:10,496 --> 01:16:13,548
listen to what I have to say, carefully.

623
01:16:16,530 --> 01:16:20,419
For these many months I've been thinking
of only defeating Ravan.

624
01:16:20,620 --> 01:16:26,011
Now my dream is about to come true,
however I have considered

625
01:16:26,011 --> 01:16:31,048
this matter over and over again and I've
concluded that I

626
01:16:31,048 --> 01:16:35,820
can stop this fight even now if my wife
Sita and other

627
01:16:35,820 --> 01:16:41,034
captives are released and they ask for
shelter under me.

628
01:16:44,017 --> 01:16:48,516
Quiet! - You are, no doubt, surprised, but
shedding of blood should

629
01:16:48,516 --> 01:16:52,814
be avoided and real peace should come back
to the three worlds.

630
01:16:53,015 --> 01:16:57,722
To ensure this I am ready to forgive and
forget the misdeeds of Ravan.

631
01:16:58,741 --> 01:17:01,652
Angad, could you carry this message to
Ravan?

632
01:17:05,612 --> 01:17:10,484
I... I understand. I will surely convey
your message to Ravan. - Thank you, Angad.

633
01:17:18,374 --> 01:17:21,286
Is that all you have to say to me?

634
01:17:22,301 --> 01:17:26,183
Well... Angad... that's your name, isn't
it?

635
01:17:27,209 --> 01:17:29,139
Here is my answer.

636
01:17:31,300 --> 01:17:33,062
How despicable!

637
01:17:33,263 --> 01:17:36,007
Is this how you treat a messenger who
comes in peace?

638
01:17:46,843 --> 01:17:53,127
Ravan Ravan, I have your answer. And now I
will carry your answer to Ram.

639
01:17:53,127 --> 01:17:57,604
Next time I see you, it will be on the
battlefield.

640
01:18:00,586 --> 01:18:03,497
So, Ravan wants war, after all.

641
01:18:03,694 --> 01:18:06,438
I understand. Angad, I appreciate your
endeavor.

642
01:18:06,639 --> 01:18:12,328
I am sorry, Ram, but Ravan did not accept
your message of peace. I did my best.

643
01:18:18,419 --> 01:18:22,481
Now, tomorrow morning when the first rays
of the sun

644
01:18:22,481 --> 01:18:26,075
touch the mountaintops the battle will
begin.

645
01:18:26,272 --> 01:18:32,936
I ask all of you present here will you
fight for justice and for Ram?

646
01:18:33,144 --> 01:18:36,870
All hail to Ram! All hail to Sugriva!

647
01:18:37,070 --> 01:18:39,814
Hail! Hail! Hail!

648
01:19:23,044 --> 01:19:25,956
Hail to the great lord of Lanka.

649
01:19:26,971 --> 01:19:29,883
Hail to the great lord of Lanka.

650
01:19:30,898 --> 01:19:34,780
If anyone tries to get in a scuffle with
Ravan...

651
01:19:34,987 --> 01:19:41,380
If anyone tries to get in a scuffle with
Ravan he is sure

652
01:19:41,380 --> 01:19:47,549
to die a dog's death. he is sure to die a
dog's death.

653
01:19:47,749 --> 01:19:51,476
Hail to the king who has ten lives.

654
01:19:52,494 --> 01:19:55,405
Hail to the king who has ten lives.

655
01:19:58,384 --> 01:20:02,266
He kills all his enemies in no time.

656
01:20:02,474 --> 01:20:06,201
He kills all the enemies!

657
01:20:06,401 --> 01:20:10,127
Hail to the king of demons!

658
01:20:10,327 --> 01:20:15,035
Hail to the king of demons!

659
01:20:18,017 --> 01:20:21,899
I pray to you, O Gods, I pray to you.

660
01:20:22,925 --> 01:20:26,808
Please... please... protect Ram. Protect
my husband.

661
01:21:22,806 --> 01:21:24,736
Oh, what a nuisance! This is bothering me.

662
01:22:03,218 --> 01:22:04,979
The day began well for us, O King.

663
01:22:05,180 --> 01:22:08,907
But now the two armies seem equally
matched.

664
01:22:09,107 --> 01:22:10,870
Our men are beginning to tire.

665
01:22:11,889 --> 01:22:15,771
Let them withdraw at once then and rest.

666
01:22:15,978 --> 01:22:19,705
Respected one, that will only lead to our
defeat.

667
01:22:19,906 --> 01:22:23,632
Let us send Kumbhakarna's sons, Kumbha and
Nikumbha.

668
01:22:24,649 --> 01:22:30,050
Tired soldiers can fall back to defense
but we shall keep up pressure on

669
01:22:30,050 --> 01:22:35,751
our enemies until sunset. - Yes, at
sunset, Ram will stop the battle for the

670
01:22:35,751 --> 01:22:41,302
day to attend to the wounded and to
cremate the dead with honor. - Good.

671
01:22:41,502 --> 01:22:44,326
I will send forth Kumbha and Nikumbha.

672
01:22:50,729 --> 01:22:53,612
Here I come... monkeys, down with you.

673
01:22:56,747 --> 01:22:58,776
I will crush you to crumbs.

674
01:23:02,938 --> 01:23:04,967
O my God!

675
01:23:26,671 --> 01:23:31,794
Monkeys I will kill you.

676
01:23:42,320 --> 01:23:46,331
Your Majesty, Kumbha and Nikumbha are
fighting with great

677
01:23:46,331 --> 01:23:48,301
courage on the battlefield.

678
01:23:48,511 --> 01:23:52,429
Well, after all, they are the sons of
Kumbhakarna.

679
01:23:56,594 --> 01:23:58,623
So many dead!

680
01:23:59,689 --> 01:24:01,718
So many wounded!

681
01:24:06,913 --> 01:24:09,973
Have you got the water ready? - Yes.

682
01:24:10,180 --> 01:24:12,032
Medicines? Herbs? - Yes, they are ready.

683
01:24:13,104 --> 01:24:16,164
Let's get the bed set fast. C'mon quickly.
- Yeah.

684
01:24:26,689 --> 01:24:29,574
Hey, more herbs.

685
01:24:30,645 --> 01:24:32,674
There are so many wounded.

686
01:24:51,282 --> 01:24:55,363
You've fought bravely. I am so proud of
you.

687
01:24:56,441 --> 01:25:02,592
Now rest. - Oh no. Such a tiny wound will
be cured by tomorrow, you will see.

688
01:25:05,727 --> 01:25:09,808
Do not strain yourself, rest. - Yes...
yes, sir.

689
01:25:25,505 --> 01:25:28,452
Brother, how could you cremate the bodies
of our enemies

690
01:25:28,452 --> 01:25:30,452
along with those of our own soldiers?

691
01:25:31,524 --> 01:25:35,604
Lakshman, they were our men and Ravan's
men while they were alive.

692
01:25:35,823 --> 01:25:38,707
But in death they are no longer enemies.

693
01:25:38,919 --> 01:25:41,802
Do they not all of them deserve a solemn
cremation?

694
01:25:42,874 --> 01:25:47,994
It is not like a true warrior a true
Kshatriya, to be moved by such emotions.

695
01:25:48,205 --> 01:25:56,249
My brother, when we set out on this
expedition I too was full of anger,
bitterness.

696
01:25:56,459 --> 01:26:00,443
But on our journey to Lanka, I've come to
see that all of

697
01:26:00,443 --> 01:26:04,496
us have received the precious gift of life
from the Gods.

698
01:26:05,747 --> 01:26:11,726
And it is more important to be a good
human being then to just be a good
Kshatriya.

699
01:26:12,969 --> 01:26:16,886
Have we not, all of us, sprung from the
same souls?

700
01:26:17,097 --> 01:26:23,076
Rakshash, vanar, men, beasts birds of the
air, the fish of the ocean...??

701
01:26:26,211 --> 01:26:30,126
Yet, some of us, in ignorance draw their
bows and swords

702
01:26:30,126 --> 01:26:32,363
against their fellow creatures.

703
01:26:34,465 --> 01:26:36,494
Many have fallen off this battlefield
today.

704
01:26:36,701 --> 01:26:39,586
And many more shall die before the war is
done.

705
01:26:39,797 --> 01:26:43,714
And as a Kshatriya, I shall continue to
fight my battles.

706
01:26:45,816 --> 01:26:51,968
But when I burn the dead, I shall pray for
a world free from all wars.

707
01:26:53,039 --> 01:26:58,159
That a man does not raise his hand in
anger against his own brother.

708
01:27:02,325 --> 01:27:04,354
Brother, words fail me.

709
01:27:39,472 --> 01:27:42,533
I am Neel, the General of the Vanaras.

710
01:27:42,739 --> 01:27:45,624
Try all you can. I shall defeat you.

711
01:28:35,191 --> 01:28:39,273
You have fought well but this is the end.

712
01:29:12,337 --> 01:29:13,334
Wait!

713
01:29:20,764 --> 01:29:23,649
Hail Sugriva! Hail Sugriva!

714
01:30:09,089 --> 01:30:12,149
Kumbha, Kumbha... my brother.

715
01:30:14,248 --> 01:30:16,276
Are you really gone?

716
01:30:20,611 --> 01:30:24,529
Is it you? Is it you who killed my brother
Kumbha?

717
01:30:25,598 --> 01:30:29,679
Yes, I am... I am Sugriva, the king of the
Vanaras.

718
01:30:29,898 --> 01:30:33,815
Your brother Kumbha was really brave and
courageous.

719
01:30:35,916 --> 01:30:38,977
I have never met such a mighty opponent
before.

720
01:30:39,184 --> 01:30:43,101
I am very impressed by his tactics. Please
cremate him in honor.

721
01:30:44,172 --> 01:30:47,511
Indrajeet, what are you saying? Prahastha
and Kumbha both

722
01:30:47,511 --> 01:30:50,323
have been killed? - It is unfortunate but
true.

723
01:30:53,458 --> 01:30:55,486
I never thought Ram's army had anyone to
match them.

724
01:30:56,554 --> 01:30:59,629
It's time to review our strategy. It can
be of help under the

725
01:30:59,629 --> 01:31:02,705
circumstances. Indrajeet, arouse
Kumbhakarna from his sleep.

726
01:31:02,917 --> 01:31:05,801
What? - Kumbha and Nikumbha fought so
hard.

727
01:31:06,012 --> 01:31:11,611
Now Kumbhakarna, their father, ten times
mightier than them can work wonders.

728
01:31:11,611 --> 01:31:16,120
Yes, I am right, wake him up immediately.
This is my command.

729
01:31:16,330 --> 01:31:18,183
All right, father. I will.

730
01:31:28,541 --> 01:31:30,569
Forward.

731
01:32:28,387 --> 01:32:30,416
C'mon... yeah...

732
01:32:53,324 --> 01:32:54,144
Oh, that big giant!

733
01:32:55,215 --> 01:32:57,243
Our lord Kumbhakarna has arrived.

734
01:33:14,820 --> 01:33:17,881
Father... father!

735
01:33:30,298 --> 01:33:34,749
Vibhishana, who is that gigantic warrior?
- That O Ram,

736
01:33:34,749 --> 01:33:39,119
is the best and the bravest warrior of
Ravan's troops.

737
01:33:39,119 --> 01:33:44,704
Kumbhakarna after six months' sleep, he
would have become immortal.

738
01:33:45,775 --> 01:33:50,374
But it seems to me that Ravan was forced
to wake up because he was in

739
01:33:50,374 --> 01:33:54,707
terror to see so many of his soldiers
killed one after the other.

740
01:33:54,707 --> 01:33:58,573
Oh yes, he needs Kumbhakarna. But even he
is not immortal.

741
01:33:58,573 --> 01:34:03,372
He is mighty enough to make all the vanara
soldiers run away in panic by

742
01:34:03,372 --> 01:34:08,437
his appearance. But Ram now is the right
moment for you to go to battle.

743
01:34:11,227 --> 01:34:13,255
Now, we go to battle.

744
01:35:25,692 --> 01:35:27,544
Jump!

745
01:35:37,902 --> 01:35:40,963
Stop that!

746
01:35:42,029 --> 01:35:44,058
You are small but you have courage.

747
01:35:48,220 --> 01:35:52,301
I am Angad, son of Bali. The nephew of
king Sugriva.

748
01:35:52,520 --> 01:35:55,404
You are kinsmen of the Vanara king!?

749
01:35:56,475 --> 01:36:02,627
No wonder you fight so great. But this is
as far as you get against me. - Wait.

750
01:36:05,934 --> 01:36:10,882
This is now my mission. I see you are
Kumbhakarna.

751
01:36:11,093 --> 01:36:13,977
The mightiest warrior of Lanka.

752
01:36:14,189 --> 01:36:18,105
Now this Hanuman is your opponent.

753
01:36:18,316 --> 01:36:21,200
Good... Good.

754
01:36:22,271 --> 01:36:24,300
But before we fight... here.

755
01:36:29,494 --> 01:36:32,555
Oh... Kumbha... Nikumbha... my sons.

756
01:36:41,876 --> 01:36:48,021
Hanuman, I thank you for your
consideration. - It is nothing.

757
01:36:58,386 --> 01:37:01,816
I won't fight you with bare hands because
you are skillful

758
01:37:01,816 --> 01:37:04,538
enough to fight with weapons in dead
earnest.

759
01:37:46,022 --> 01:37:48,907
It was good for you that I lost my mace.

760
01:37:49,118 --> 01:37:50,971
Now get up and fight.

761
01:37:51,181 --> 01:37:54,066
Wait... stop wherever you are.

762
01:37:54,277 --> 01:37:58,194
I am Ram, the Prince of Ayodhya, son of
Dashrath.

763
01:38:14,742 --> 01:38:16,770
Give away, you stupid fools!

764
01:38:18,009 --> 01:38:20,893
So you are Ram!?

765
01:38:21,965 --> 01:38:25,025
You are a skillful swordsman, I hear.

766
01:38:25,232 --> 01:38:27,084
You are annoying me.

767
01:38:28,156 --> 01:38:31,216
Go away, play with the monkeys.

768
01:38:40,537 --> 01:38:46,770
It has grown dark and even with
Kumbhakarna on the field the battle goes

769
01:38:46,770 --> 01:38:47,721
on and on.

770
01:38:47,933 --> 01:38:50,817
Father, I will go to the battlefield and
bring you the report.

771
01:38:51,029 --> 01:38:52,881
Yes Indrajeet, my son, go.

772
01:39:25,939 --> 01:39:30,020
Excuse me Kumbhakarna, I am only doing my
duty.

773
01:39:48,639 --> 01:39:50,668
He has done it! He has done it.

774
01:39:51,735 --> 01:39:53,764
Hail to the Prince of Ayodhya!

775
01:39:55,862 --> 01:39:59,944
Brother, are you well? It has been a
glorious deed!

776
01:40:01,021 --> 01:40:05,103
Yes... I am hurt but well in spirit.

777
01:40:05,321 --> 01:40:08,205
I wish I had known him as a friend.

778
01:40:08,417 --> 01:40:11,301
Vibhishana, I am sorry, Kumbhakarna had to
die at my hands.

779
01:40:20,626 --> 01:40:23,687
Save us... save us O Vanaras.

780
01:40:30,945 --> 01:40:34,005
Thank you, Lord Ram!

781
01:40:34,212 --> 01:40:36,065
Ram, the great!

782
01:40:37,135 --> 01:40:40,196
Freedom, at last!

783
01:40:42,295 --> 01:40:44,324
We are free!

784
01:40:44,531 --> 01:40:47,415
What? Even Kumbhakarna is gone?

785
01:40:47,627 --> 01:40:50,510
This spells disaster for Lanka.

786
01:40:50,722 --> 01:40:53,606
He was a fine warrior.

787
01:40:54,677 --> 01:40:57,737
It is sad, very sad.

788
01:40:57,945 --> 01:41:00,829
Father... don't despair. Have faith.

789
01:41:01,040 --> 01:41:03,924
I have a plan.

790
01:41:04,136 --> 01:41:08,053
I will devastate Ram's troops. I assure
you of this.

791
01:41:09,123 --> 01:41:13,204
Well said, my son, well said. My faith
lies in you.

792
01:41:14,282 --> 01:41:16,311
Now go ahead. - Yes, father.

793
01:41:17,549 --> 01:41:20,434
Let us bring all of them in, while it is
still dark.

794
01:41:20,645 --> 01:41:22,498
Hurry... hurry.

795
01:41:26,837 --> 01:41:30,753
There will be many more corpses for you to
gather, my friend.

796
01:41:30,964 --> 01:41:34,881
How dare he speak this way? I will show
him.

797
01:41:35,091 --> 01:41:36,943
Wait! What is that?

798
01:41:41,282 --> 01:41:43,134
That is Sita.

799
01:41:49,365 --> 01:41:52,425
Hanuman, are you alright? Angad!?

800
01:42:00,715 --> 01:42:04,796
Where is Ram? Why is he such a coward?

801
01:42:06,906 --> 01:42:09,966
Ram... Ram...

802
01:42:11,034 --> 01:42:13,062
Sita... my queen!

803
01:42:15,161 --> 01:42:17,189
Here you are.

804
01:42:18,429 --> 01:42:20,280
Ram, watch carefully.

805
01:42:26,683 --> 01:42:30,601
Stop! Stop! STOP!

806
01:42:35,969 --> 01:42:40,919
Sita... Sita!

807
01:42:53,511 --> 01:42:58,459
Lakshman come... come... come over here.

808
01:43:05,893 --> 01:43:10,179
Before I dispose of you, Ram, I will give
you enough time

809
01:43:10,179 --> 01:43:13,938
to hold a funeral for your wife and your
brother.

810
01:43:22,402 --> 01:43:24,255
Sita!

811
01:43:32,721 --> 01:43:35,605
May I talk with you for a moment?

812
01:43:35,817 --> 01:43:39,733
We have almost used up all the herbs
around in this area.

813
01:43:39,944 --> 01:43:43,860
But they don't heal the wounds inflicted
by Indrajeet, at all.

814
01:43:44,071 --> 01:43:47,989
What? What news is this? - O God!

815
01:43:49,058 --> 01:43:53,356
Oh... I have already lost my beloved wife
Sita and now...

816
01:43:53,356 --> 01:43:57,275
I am going to lose my dear, dear brother,
Lakshman.

817
01:43:58,344 --> 01:44:00,374
If I lose him, what else would be left for
me?

818
01:44:03,504 --> 01:44:06,564
Brace yourself, Ram. You cannot grieve and
fret like this.

819
01:44:06,772 --> 01:44:10,378
Your despair will damage the morale of our
troops more

820
01:44:10,378 --> 01:44:13,784
than the enemy's arrows. Please do not
worry, Ram.

821
01:44:13,995 --> 01:44:21,007
Sita surely must be alive. - Alive? But I
saw Sita slain before my own eyes.

822
01:44:21,218 --> 01:44:25,134
I know, it must be one of Indrajeet's
magic tricks.

823
01:44:25,345 --> 01:44:28,229
A magic trick? What? - Yes.

824
01:44:28,440 --> 01:44:31,325
And we must not allow his tricks to
perplex us.

825
01:44:31,536 --> 01:44:33,389
Your grief will only give him strength.

826
01:44:34,459 --> 01:44:38,540
Indrajeet's strength lies in his magical
powers.

827
01:44:38,758 --> 01:44:42,935
The only way to take his powers away from
him is to attack Indrajeet

828
01:44:42,935 --> 01:44:46,804
while he performs his Tantrik rites in the
cave of Nikumbhila.

829
01:44:47,014 --> 01:44:50,931
Indrajeet makes it a rule to perform a
religious ceremony.

830
01:44:51,141 --> 01:44:54,025
He offers sacrifices to the Goddess
Nikumbhila.

831
01:44:54,237 --> 01:44:57,120
From the evening hours way until
nightfall.

832
01:44:57,332 --> 01:45:01,249
He gains his extraordinary magical powers
through this ceremony.

833
01:45:02,319 --> 01:45:06,646
I see, now... we still have so many
soldiers wounded,

834
01:45:06,646 --> 01:45:09,503
my brother Lakshman, for instance.

835
01:45:10,574 --> 01:45:16,726
No, I think it would be very hard for us
to attack Nikumbhila cave now. - Ram.

836
01:45:18,828 --> 01:45:24,552
In... in the Himalayas... - Yes the
Himalayas what about them?

837
01:45:24,552 --> 01:45:27,045
Rest, Jamvant. Talk to me.

838
01:45:29,147 --> 01:45:34,299
I know there are some herbs there that can
heal our wounds,

839
01:45:34,299 --> 01:45:37,355
in the Himalayas. - The Himalayas?

840
01:45:39,638 --> 01:45:42,521
I am afraid... I am afraid that is too far
away.

841
01:46:31,057 --> 01:46:36,170
I see... that must be Ram's kingdom!
Ayodhya!

842
01:46:44,471 --> 01:46:46,500
The Himalayas!

843
01:46:49,631 --> 01:46:51,659
O you Himalayas!

844
01:46:52,898 --> 01:46:56,815
Sacred mountains! At last!

845
01:47:46,382 --> 01:47:48,411
Ah Dronagiri, at last!

846
01:47:57,904 --> 01:48:00,789
Now, I have to look for herbs.

847
01:48:00,999 --> 01:48:03,884
Our army is in desperate need of this.

848
01:48:09,255 --> 01:48:12,139
Ah the herbs... there they are.

849
01:48:19,573 --> 01:48:22,457
Uff... that was painful.

850
01:48:36,082 --> 01:48:40,000
Good, the pain is gone. I am healed.

851
01:48:40,209 --> 01:48:44,127
These herbs were far better than I ever
expected.

852
01:48:49,324 --> 01:48:55,476
But wait! Just a handful of these herbs
won't be enough to heal them all.

853
01:48:57,579 --> 01:49:00,639
Now... let me think.

854
01:49:06,865 --> 01:49:09,926
I will take one. Yes, this tree is good
enough.

855
01:49:51,407 --> 01:49:53,259
This will be a landmark.

856
01:50:04,648 --> 01:50:10,800
Now I will pick up the whole mountain.

857
01:50:43,858 --> 01:50:50,010
I pray to you O Gods! Protect my master
Lakshman I am coming back with the herbs.

858
01:50:52,286 --> 01:50:57,234
Brother Lakshman, keep up your fight for
life a little longer.

859
01:51:04,495 --> 01:51:07,684
Bear your pain with courage, Lakshman.
Take heart Hanuman

860
01:51:07,684 --> 01:51:10,648
will soon be back with the herbs that will
heal you.

861
01:51:17,909 --> 01:51:23,022
Ram... Ram... - Lakshman... Lakshman.

862
01:51:24,100 --> 01:51:28,182
There he is. - Hanuman has come. - Hail!
Hail!

863
01:51:29,260 --> 01:51:33,341
Here comes Hanuman! - But what has he got
on his shoulders?

864
01:51:34,419 --> 01:51:37,479
He is carrying something. - That's a
mountain he is carrying.

865
01:51:37,687 --> 01:51:41,603
Along with the herbs, he has brought the
whole mountain.

866
01:52:00,214 --> 01:52:03,275
Hanuman, the herbs are on this mountain? -
Yes.

867
01:52:03,482 --> 01:52:07,399
Look for the landmarks where I have stuck
trees to the soil.

868
01:52:07,610 --> 01:52:10,494
Hurry, apply the herbs to Lakshman's
wounds.

869
01:52:11,565 --> 01:52:14,625
Yes, it's a miracle.

870
01:52:20,852 --> 01:52:23,912
Herbs... herbs. - At last.

871
01:52:32,202 --> 01:52:37,322
Brother Ram... - O Lakshman you have
regained consciousness.

872
01:52:41,660 --> 01:52:44,545
Hanuman, you too are a beloved brother to
me.

873
01:52:51,807 --> 01:52:54,867
Hey... - Who is that?

874
01:53:10,380 --> 01:53:12,409
Hey... what was that?

875
01:53:19,666 --> 01:53:21,695
C'mon... c'mon.

876
01:54:03,176 --> 01:54:05,028
What has happened?

877
01:54:07,132 --> 01:54:09,160
Oh no... who is there?

878
01:54:10,227 --> 01:54:13,287
Is it you? You are still alive.

879
01:54:14,354 --> 01:54:19,467
Yes, and it is time for you to die along
with your guardian Goddess.

880
01:54:23,813 --> 01:54:27,073
It is hard to believe that even such one
as you can have

881
01:54:27,073 --> 01:54:28,760
faithful slaves to save you.

882
01:54:29,832 --> 01:54:32,892
All of you, kill him.

883
01:55:03,883 --> 01:55:05,912
What a nuisance!

884
01:55:12,137 --> 01:55:14,166
You... take me up there!

885
01:55:46,188 --> 01:55:52,341
Indrajeet... - I am not so stupid to be
trapped by a monkey like you!

886
01:56:01,665 --> 01:56:03,694
He has slipped past.

887
01:56:14,048 --> 01:56:18,129
Listen, you obey my commands and I'll
spare your life.

888
01:56:18,347 --> 01:56:23,299
Carry me to the sky. Remember you should
head right, when I say right and

889
01:56:23,299 --> 01:56:28,454
left when I say left. If you fail to do so
this sword will cut your throat.

890
01:56:51,194 --> 01:56:53,222
Lakshman... !!?

891
01:56:54,290 --> 01:56:57,350
Just keep going... and faster... faster.

892
01:56:58,417 --> 01:57:00,445
I will kill you.

893
01:57:04,608 --> 01:57:06,637
Not this time. This time I will kill you.

894
01:57:20,085 --> 01:57:22,114
You cannot destroy this.

895
01:57:33,672 --> 01:57:37,588
But this is the end of you.

896
01:57:39,691 --> 01:57:41,719
This is your end, not mine.

897
01:57:45,882 --> 01:57:47,911
I've waited for this moment.

898
01:57:53,104 --> 01:57:55,133
Got you, you little one.

899
01:58:13,742 --> 01:58:16,801
This is the end of the invincible
Indrajeet.

900
01:58:18,901 --> 01:58:22,981
No... never... I wouldn't let you kill me.

901
01:58:42,632 --> 01:58:45,693
O Indrajeet... my son.

902
01:58:45,900 --> 01:58:49,747
My beloved son slew an illusion of Sita.

903
01:58:49,960 --> 01:58:52,875
I shall not slay the real one.

904
01:58:53,089 --> 01:58:57,048
Anyone so devoted to Ram deserves to die.

905
01:58:58,130 --> 01:59:01,223
Will you now add to your sins by killing
Sita!?

906
01:59:01,433 --> 01:59:03,305
An innocent woman!?

907
01:59:03,519 --> 01:59:08,703
Look at Prahastha, look at Kumbha...
Nikumbha and Kumbhakarna.

908
01:59:08,703 --> 01:59:12,716
Each one fought bravely and died a hero's
death.

909
01:59:12,716 --> 01:59:16,980
Even Indrajeet died in battle. You who are
brother,

910
01:59:16,980 --> 01:59:22,080
father king to them all do you want
disgrace their memory?

911
01:59:22,293 --> 01:59:27,295
The time has come for both of us to go
forth and avenge our kinsmen.

912
01:59:29,421 --> 01:59:33,152
I understand. But you will stay here and
protect our women and children.

913
01:59:33,152 --> 01:59:35,639
No power on earth can crush me. Not even
Ram's.

914
02:00:29,916 --> 02:00:31,967
Fire and damnation!

915
02:00:52,863 --> 02:00:54,913
He looks like Vishnu himself on his
Garuda.

916
02:00:55,123 --> 02:00:56,995
You are right, he does.

917
02:01:33,541 --> 02:01:37,666
This battle between you and me shall be
the end of it all.

918
02:01:37,887 --> 02:01:40,802
Citizens of Lanka, take heed.

919
02:01:41,885 --> 02:01:46,064
Your king Ravan, whom you consider a
symbol of eternal power,

920
02:01:46,064 --> 02:01:49,147
watch him die at the hands of a mere
mortal.

921
02:01:50,229 --> 02:01:54,354
Ram, just tell me where your conceit comes
from, huh?

922
02:01:54,575 --> 02:01:58,535
Your boastful lips will never speak such
words again.

923
02:01:58,747 --> 02:02:06,878
Brave soldiers of Lanka you know only too
well who is the mightiest of all, here!

924
02:02:07,091 --> 02:02:10,007
C'mon Ran...

925
02:02:10,221 --> 02:02:13,136
So be it, Ravan! Fight!

926
02:03:04,284 --> 02:03:06,334
Incredible!

927
02:03:12,802 --> 02:03:14,675
Now, he is dead.

928
02:03:37,661 --> 02:03:40,754
I can't believe my own eyes.

929
02:03:44,962 --> 02:03:47,012
You thought I was finished, did you?

930
02:03:50,177 --> 02:03:53,271
I would like to lay my hands on you!

931
02:04:20,425 --> 02:04:22,475
Let's see you get out of that one.

932
02:04:42,328 --> 02:04:45,422
What power is this, greater than mine?

933
02:04:53,976 --> 02:04:56,891
Oh, you are going too far now, I tell you.

934
02:05:20,920 --> 02:05:22,971
Don't you dare!

935
02:05:28,221 --> 02:05:30,272
Give up, Ram... give up!

936
02:05:57,426 --> 02:06:00,520
Om... peace... peace... peace!!!

937
02:06:48,534 --> 02:06:53,703
May you rest in peace, brother Ravan. - It
is all over.

938
02:07:01,051 --> 02:07:06,219
Soldiers of Lanka, king Ravan has gone
back to mother Earth.

939
02:07:07,309 --> 02:07:12,597
Give up fighting. Lay down your arms and
devote yourself to

940
02:07:12,597 --> 02:07:18,601
restoring the glory of your country with
your new king Vibhishana.

941
02:07:22,643 --> 02:07:24,611
Ram...

942
02:07:38,659 --> 02:07:40,627
Sita! - Ram!

943
02:07:50,671 --> 02:07:54,237
Thank you all, but when I think of the
people who died

944
02:07:54,237 --> 02:07:58,001
for me I feel sad. I will meditate and
will pray for them

945
02:07:58,001 --> 02:08:00,643
from now on and beg their forgiveness.

946
02:08:01,682 --> 02:08:03,650
You don't need to do that.

947
02:08:03,851 --> 02:08:08,651
All you need is to live in peace with Ram
to make their death a glorious sacrifice.

948
02:08:08,856 --> 02:08:11,654
I will remember what you said, Sugriva.

949
02:08:14,695 --> 02:08:18,979
Vibhishana, the new king of Lanka presents
Ram and Sita the Vimana,

950
02:08:18,979 --> 02:08:21,664
the flying chariot, to return to Ayodhya.

951
02:08:44,725 --> 02:08:48,684
As they return, Sita gazes at Ram with
mixed feelings.

952
02:08:48,896 --> 02:08:53,696
Happy to be reunited with him after a long
period of separation.

953
02:08:53,901 --> 02:08:59,702
And sorrowful too for the precious lives
lost for her sake in the avoidable war.

954
02:09:10,751 --> 02:09:14,464
Ayodhya celebrates the safe return of
their beloved king

955
02:09:14,464 --> 02:09:16,719
and they live happily thereafter.

956
02:09:16,924 --> 02:09:21,724
A few years later, Ram returns to the
Heavens while Sita returns to Mother
Earth.
